course: dictionary
lesson: 5378
title: Kneel and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To kneel is to go down so that one or both knees rest on the ground. It is a doing word, a verb, and it changes its form depending on the time: kneels, knelt or kneeled, kneeling. You do not need a dictionary to get the main idea, because the words around it give you clues.
explain: Look at «At the zoo a camel kneels with its humps wobbling.» The camel is doing something low down, and the word kneels tells you it is going down onto its knees. Now try your meaning in the sentence: "a camel goes down with its knees on the ground" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The same clue appears in «The Hatter, kneeling, says he can't go any lower.» He is already down low, so kneeling must mean being on his knees. Read the whole sentence, not just the hard word, and the meaning becomes clear.
explain: Kneel is used in many places: buses kneel down at the stop, and a newborn calf kneels to drink. In a story, a knight may kneel before a king. When you meet a new verb, ask: what is the action, and who or what is doing it?
fact: Kneel means to go down with one or both knees on the ground.
fact: The forms are kneel, kneels, knelt or kneeled, and kneeling.
fact: Kneel down, kneel beside and on bended knee are common phrases.
fact: «A newborn calf... kneels to drink with its mouth.»
fact: «Many buses kneel down at the stop by lowering their suspension.»
exercise: «At the zoo a camel kneels with its humps wobbling.» What does kneels mean? | *Goes down with its knees on the ground | Runs very fast | Eats all its food | Jumps high into the air
exercise: Find and copy the word in «The Hatter, kneeling, says he can't go any lower» that means going down onto the knees. | *kneeling | stand | King | lower
exercise: Yesterday Sam ___ down to tie his shoelace. Which word fits the gap? | kneeling | kneels | *knelt | kneel
test: «Many buses kneel down at the stop by lowering their suspension.» What does kneel down mean for a bus? | *Lower itself close to the ground at the stop | Carry more people on its roof | Turn off its engine at the stop | Drive very fast over the bumps
test: In stories, a knight ___ before the king to show respect. Which word fits the gap? | sings | flies | sleeps | *kneels
exam: Ella says the camel kneels because it is tired. What is the best way to check her meaning? | *Swap in "goes down with its knees on the ground" and see if the sentence still makes sense | Decide that kneel means jumping | Look up how many legs a camel has only | Count the humps to see if she is right
